<!--
  The AdMob application id.

  Not optional once the ads SDK is on the classpath: it is read out of the
  manifest when the app starts, and a build without it crashes on launch
  rather than merely failing to show an ad.

  The value below is Google's public test app id. It pairs with the test ad
  units in lib/data/ads.dart and serves placeholder ads to any device, which
  is what makes the whole thing testable without an account.

  Before shipping, all three have to change together:
    1. this id, from AdMob -> your app -> App settings,
    2. the two ad unit ids in lib/data/ads.dart,
    3. GADApplicationIdentifier in ios/Runner/Info.plist.

  Mixing them is the expensive mistake. A real app id with test units earns
  nothing; a test app id with real units serves nothing; and developing
  against real units is what gets an AdMob account suspended for invalid
  traffic, because Google counts those impressions as fraud.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="admob_app_id" translatable="false">ca-app-pub-3940256099942544~3347511713</string>
</resources>
